.TH HEARTBEAT_CONFIG.YAML 5 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-heartbeatmonitor t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
heartbeat_config.yaml \- heartbeat monitor configuration file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I config/heartbeat_config.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML mapping read by
.BR heartbeat_monitor.py (1)
via
.BR \-c / \-\-config .
Each top\-level section is merged one level deep over the built\-in defaults;
keys not given keep their defaults.
A section key that is present but empty (for example
.B monitor:
with every entry commented out) parses as null and aborts startup with a
Python
.BR TypeError ;
delete the key instead.
A YAML syntax error also aborts startup with a traceback.
.B CRS_PORT_HTTP
and
.B CRS_PORT_UDP
in the environment override the ports after the file is read.
.SS server
.TP
.B udp_host
IPv4 bind address.
Default
.BR 0.0.0.0 .
.TP
.B udp_port
UDP heartbeat port, IPv4.
Default 9999.
.TP
.B web_host
HTTP bind address.
Default
.BR 0.0.0.0 .
.TP
.B web_port
HTTP port.
Built\-in default 8080; the shipped file says 5003; the control room overrides
it to 8081 through
.BR CRS_PORT_HTTP .
Both 8080 (resource\-manager) and 5003 (fts) are used by other services.
.TP
.B multicast_groups
List of IPv4 multicast group addresses to join.
Default empty.
.TP
.B ipv6_enabled
Start the IPv6 listener.
Default true.
.TP
.B udp6_host
IPv6 bind address.
Default
.BR :: .
The socket is
.BR IPV6_V6ONLY ,
so it may share the port number with
.BR udp_port .
.TP
.B udp6_port
UDP heartbeat port, IPv6.
Default 9999.
.TP
.B multicast6_groups
List of mappings
.B {group: \fIaddress\fP, interface: \fIname\fP}
to join.
.B interface
is required for link\-local groups such as
.BR ff02::1 .
.SS monitor
.TP
.B default_timeout
Seconds without a heartbeat before a sender is shown timed out.
Built\-in default 30; shipped file 60.
.TP
.B cleanup_after
Seconds without a heartbeat before a sender is removed from the display and
from
.B /api/health
counts.
Built\-in default 300; shipped file 86400.
Applies to configured senders as well.
.TP
.B refresh_interval
Seconds between Server\-Sent Events updates.
Default 2.
.TP
.B grid_columns
Dashboard columns, 1 to 6.
Default 3.
.TP
.B theme
.B dark
or
.BR light .
Default
.BR dark .
.SS daemon
.TP
.B enabled
Run as a daemon without
.BR \-\-daemon .
Default false.
.TP
.B pid_file
Default
.IR /tmp/heartbeat_monitor.pid .
.TP
.B log_file
Default
.IR /tmp/heartbeat_monitor.log .
.TP
.B working_dir
Directory to change to after forking.
Default
.IR / .
.SS systems
Optional list of per\-sender overrides:
.TP
.B name
Sender name, matched exactly against the heartbeat
.B name
field.
.TP
.B timeout
Timeout in seconds for this sender.
.TP
.B description
Text shown under the name on the dashboard.
.PP
Listing a sender here does not make the monitor expect it: a listed sender
that never sends a heartbeat is not displayed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
server:
  udp_port: 9999
  web_port: 8081
  ipv6_enabled: true
monitor:
  default_timeout: 60
  cleanup_after: 86400
systems:
  \- name: "runcontrol"
    timeout: 10
    description: "Run control heartbeat"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR heartbeat_monitor.py (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor\-api (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
